# Exclude **every** node_modules (pnpm install already ran inside the image
# before COPY . .).
# Each workspace package besides the root has its own: pnpm creates
# packages/<pkg>/node_modules (symlinks into the root .pnpm store) for any
# package that declares deps. Under npm only packages/web had one (the rest
# relied on hoisting), so the old list only named that — after the migration
# agent/server/cli/protocol all have them too. Without excluding them, COPY . .
# would bring the host darwin symlink trees into the linux image (platform
# binaries mixed into the dep tree, very hard to debug). The in-image copies
# come from install; excluding the copy does not affect resolution.
/node_modules
/packages/protocol/node_modules
/packages/cli/node_modules
/packages/agent/node_modules
/packages/server/node_modules
/packages/web/node_modules
/dist
/packages/web/dist
/data
/temp
/.git
# Tooling and tests: unused at build time (tsc only compiles packages/*/src);
# keep them out of the image context
/.codebuddy
/.cursor
/.agents
/docs
/tests
*.png
*.log
lifeline.sqlite*
.env
.env.development
